>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Choice of Bluetooth Versus LoRa)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Bluetooth was ruled out for the rural deployment due to its limited range. Instead, LoRa was selected because its long-range, low-power capabilities are ideal for village-scale monitoring systems that require reliable data transmission over long distances.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Choice for the number of pressure sensors to detect pipe leak)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Initially, a single pressure sensor was considered for leak detection. However, it could incorrectly identify normal pressure fluctuations as leaks, leading to false positives. Therefore, a two-sensor approach was adopted to improve detection accuracy and enable more reliable identification of actual leaks.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
425 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Backing up sensor data)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Relying solely on live LoRa transmissions risks data loss due to rural power outages, gateway downtime, or signal interference. To ensure data integrity, a local SD card logging mechanism was introduced. By saving time-stamped sensor logs directly on-site, the system guarantees zero data loss during network blind spots and allows authorities to retrieve historical data for offline analysis.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Introducing the concept of weighted average cumulative score)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Instead of displaying raw sensor readings, a weighted average cumulative score was introduced to simplify decision making for villagers. Each water quality parameter is assigned a weight based on its relative impact on water safety. The individual contributions are then combined to generate a single score. If the score exceeds a predetermined threshold, the water is classified as safe for drinking; otherwise, an alert is generated.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
